# ScriptedController.ChooseTargets never validates its queued answer against
# the offered candidates (last pack's own header note, targeting-and-chaining.md).
# CR 702.11b: Leyline of Sanctity's own continuous grant (`Affected$ You |
# AddKeyword$ Hexproof`) puts Hexproof on human, not on any card --
# applyOneContinuousKeyword's own new player branch (continuous.go) writes
# it to Player.KeywordMod every Layer 6 pass. ai's Lightning Bolt at human
# is still offered a legal candidate (ai itself, ValidTgts$ Any), so casting
# still succeeds; the CR 608.2b re-check (targetStillLegal ->
# playerCantBeTargetedBy) then finds human illegal and drops it -- Bolt
# fizzles, dealing no damage.
startturn ai
advance 3
tapformana ai 2 R
queue targets human
queue action ai cast 3
passpriority
